<span class="ltx_author_before">  </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Laith Zumot
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span>Nokia
</span>
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_email"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Email: </span><a href="mailto:"><span id="id6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">laith.zumot@nokia.com</span></a>
</span></span></span></span></div>

<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p">The rise of large reasoning language models (LRLMs) has unlocked new potential for solving complex tasks. These models operate with a thinking budget, that is, a predefined number of reasoning tokens used to arrive at a solution.</p>
    
<p id="abstract1.2" class="ltx_p">We propose a novel approach, inspired by the generator/discriminator framework in generative adversarial networks, in which a critic model periodically probes its own reasoning to assess whether it has reached a confident conclusion. If not, reasoning continues until a target certainty threshold is met. This mechanism adaptively balances efficiency and reliability by allowing early termination when confidence is high, while encouraging further reasoning when uncertainty persists.</p>
    
<p id="abstract1.3" class="ltx_p">Through experiments on the AIME2024 and AIME2025 datasets, we show that Certainty-Guided Reasoning (CGR) improves baseline accuracy while reducing token usage. Importantly, extended multi-seed evaluations over 64 runs demonstrate that CGR is stable, reducing variance across seeds and improving exam-like performance under penalty-based grading. Additionally, our token savings analysis shows that CGR can eliminate millions of tokens in aggregate, with tunable trade-offs between certainty thresholds and efficiency.</p>
    
<p id="abstract1.4" class="ltx_p">Together, these findings highlight certainty as a powerful signal for reasoning sufficiency. By integrating confidence into the reasoning process, CGR makes large reasoning language models more adaptive, trustworthy, and resource efficient, paving the way for practical deployment in domains where both accuracy and computational cost matter.</p>
  
</div>
<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1 </span>Introduction</h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Large language models (LLMs) have demonstrated remarkable capabilities across a broad range of natural language understanding and generation tasks. As these models continue to evolve, a new class of systems—large reasoning language models (LRLMs)—has emerged, designed specifically to tackle complex, multi-step reasoning problems. These models often operate within a fixed thinking budget, that is, the number of tokens allocated for internal reasoning before producing an output. While this thinking budget is critical for enabling structured thinking, it introduces a trade-off: allocating too little thinking budget may lead to premature or incorrect conclusions, whereas allocating too much can result in wasted computation and reduced efficiency <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al. (2025)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In this work, we introduce a novel method called Certainty-Guided Reasoning (CGR), which calculates model certainty within the reasoning process of LRLMs and
adaptively determines when to stop thinking based on the model’s confidence in its answer.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Inspired by the generator/discriminator architecture in generative adversarial networks (GANs) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Goodfellow et al. (2014)</a></cite>,
we propose a method in which a critic model periodically evaluates the generated reasoning trace to determine if its current state justifies termination. This certainty-guided mechanism allows the model to use reasoning resources more effectively, focusing effort only where needed.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Our key insight is that the certainty can serve as a signal for reasoning sufficiency—if the model is confident in its current answer, further reasoning may be unnecessary. Conversely, if uncertainty remains high, the model should continue reasoning to refine its solution.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">This evaluation framework underscores the importance of encouraging models not only to answer correctly, but also to know when not to answer at all. If a LLMs can reliably detect when they are uncertain, this capability could serve as a powerful safeguard against confidently incorrect answers. While supervised learning methods can be used to train models to abstain to answer in the face of uncertainty (see e.g. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kadavath et al. (2022)</a></cite>), they depend on curated datasets that explicitly include both typical and atypical inputs. However, exposing a model to such “out-of-distribution” examples during training inherently reclassifies them as in-distribution, undermining the robustness of this strategy. In situations that are entirely new and unfamiliar to the model—where it has neither encountered nor estimated them—these methods might not succeed. A more robust approach involves providing the model with internal systems that can identify when it is functioning outside its comfort zone, regardless of any previous experience with similar data.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">By incorporating model certainty as a first-class component of the reasoning process, we offer a step toward more adaptive, resource-efficient, and intelligent language model behavior.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Related Work</h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As LLMs are increasingly applied to complex reasoning tasks, recent work has focused on improving inference efficiency through dynamic token allocation and early stopping mechanisms. Our work builds on this growing body of research, introducing a certainty-guided framework that adapts the amount of reasoning a model performs based on its internal confidence in its answer.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A particularly relevant direction is explored in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al. (2025)</a></cite>, which proposes a method for halting the reasoning process when the model is sufficiently confident in its answer. Their approach demonstrates that dynamically stopping reasoning based on confidence can both reduce computation and improve performance. Our work follows a similar philosophy, but differs in a some ways, we introduce a dedicated probing mechanism to monitor certainty during generation, taking the minimum certainty of the tokens instead of the average, and we integrate budget forcing <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Muennighoff et al. (2025)</a></cite></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Budget forcing consists of appending “Wait" tokens to encourage the model to continue reasoning. Their results show that pushing the model to reason longer improves performance on mathematical tasks. We adopt a similar strategy, but add a certainty-aware layer to avoid unnecessary continuation when the model is already confident, effectively combining their technique with a dynamic stopping rule.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Complementary to these works, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al. (2024)</a></cite> proposes a method for dynamically determining how many reasoning samples to draw at inference time. Rather than relying on a fixed number of outputs for self-consistency, their approach adapts sampling based on convergence signals. Although we do not use self-consistency sampling, our probing mechanism similarly evaluates when enough information has been gathered—using model certainty instead of output agreement as the decision signal.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">More architectural approaches such as <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Elhoushi et al. (2024)</a></cite> focus on enabling early exits by allowing models to terminate inference at earlier layers when confident. While their work emphasizes efficiency during training and decoding at the layer level, we focus on reasoning-level decisions made during inference. Both works, however, share the goal of making LLM inference more adaptive and computationally efficient.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, broader studies on neural scaling laws have shown that increasing test-time computation—rather than model size alone—can yield significant performance gains. These insights support our strategy of using longer reasoning trajectories when needed, rather than enforcing a one-size-fits-all thinking budget. Our certainty-based approach provides a lightweight, task-sensitive method for determining when additional compute is justified.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Together, these works demonstrate a growing interest in adaptive reasoning strategies for LLMs. Our contribution lies in combining certainty estimation, budget forcing, and periodic probing to allow models to reason just enough—stopping early when confident, and continuing when needed. This balance, especially in high-stakes domains like math problem solving, offers a promising path toward more efficient and accurate large reasoning language models.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Methodology</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section details the methods used to evaluate and improve reasoning in LRLMs through dynamic thinking budgets and certainty-guided reasoning. We describe our baseline setup, introduce techniques such as budget forcing and certainty probing, and explain how these components interact during inference. Our evaluations are conducted on the AIME2024 and AIME2025 dataset, which each includes 30 math problems with integer answers in the range [0, 999].</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>Baseline Setup</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the baseline, we provide the questions to the model (<span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-14B</span>, <span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Phi-4-reasoning-plus</span>, and <span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Qwen3-14B</span>)
to generate reasoning tokens until before it predicts the designated “end of thinking" token (&lt;/think&gt;) or the end-of-sequence. After this, we append "&lt;/think&gt;Final Answer: <code id="S3.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">\boxed{</code>" to the output and extract the predicted answer. We evaluate performance by comparing these predictions to ground truth answers from the dataset.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Certainty-Guided Reasoning and Answer Extraction</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            Question <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, Model <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, Budget <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, Certainty threshold <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            Initialize output <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
            Initialize token count <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&lt;B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&lt;B</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
              Generate next token <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\leftarrow\mathcal{M}(q,o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\leftarrow\mathcal{M}(q,o)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
              Append token: <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\leftarrow o\mathbin{\|}x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\leftarrow o\mathbin{\|}x</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leftarrow t+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leftarrow t+1</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;\thinking&gt;</span> <span id="alg1.l8.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
               <span id="alg1.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">break</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
              
              Compute certainty <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\leftarrow\textsc{CertaintyProbe}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">CertaintyProbe</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\leftarrow\textsc{CertaintyProbe}(o)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\geq\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\geq\theta</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l12.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
              
              
               <span id="alg1.l13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">break</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l14.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l15.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">16:</span></span>
              
              
            Append <span id="alg1.l16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">‘‘Final Answer: \boxed{"</span> to <math id="alg1.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg1.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ExtractAnswer</span>(<math id="alg1.l17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math>)

</div>
<div id="alg1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l18.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">18:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg1.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To analyze performance under varying computational limits, we run the model with different fixed token budgets: 1000, 2000, 3000, …, up to 32,000 tokens. Note that each model has their own recommended settings and recommended prompts but we decided to run a simple system prompt ("You are a helpful assistant") and temperature <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> for consistency. Similarly to the Berkeley Function Calling Leaderboard evaluation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Patil et al. (2023)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Budget Forcing</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We observed that models often produce answers well before exhausting their allocated token budget. For example, in a 32k-token run, some answers appeared after 4k tokens. While this appears to conserve resources, it may miss opportunities for revision or deeper reasoning.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To encourage further exploration, we introduce budget forcing, which prevents premature halting. If the model attempts to terminate early (i.e., by outputting the end-of-thinking token), we substitute it with "\nWait". This forces the model to keep reasoning, sometimes leading to answer changes and improvements.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">However, budget forcing is conditional: if the model reaches an answer early and its certainty is high (see below), we allow it to stop. Otherwise, we force it to reason further.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Our Budget Forcing Implementation</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            Question <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, Model <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, Budget <math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            Initialize output <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
            Initialize token count <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&lt;B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&lt;B</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
              Generate next token <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\leftarrow\mathcal{M}(q,o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\leftarrow\mathcal{M}(q,o)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\texttt{&lt;/think&gt;}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">&lt;/think&gt;</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\texttt{&lt;/think&gt;}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> “<span id="alg2.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">\nWait</span>”

</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
              Append token: <math id="alg2.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\leftarrow o\mathbin{\|}x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\leftarrow o\mathbin{\|}x</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="alg2.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leftarrow t+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leftarrow t+1</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
              
              
            Append <span id="alg2.l12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">‘‘Final Answer: \boxed{’’</span> to <math id="alg2.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg2.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ExtractAnswer</span>(<math id="alg2.l13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math>)

</div>
<div id="alg2.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg2.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Certainty Estimation and Threshold Calibration</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In large language models, next-token prediction is based on a vector of logits representing unnormalized token scores. These logits are passed through a softmax function to produce a probability distribution over the vocabulary. The concentration of the softmax output reflects the model’s certainty.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This equation defines the probability distribution <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(t_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(t_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> over the next token <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, obtained by applying the softmax function to the output of the model <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>. The model takes as input the prompt <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>, task description <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, auxiliary input <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math>, and the sequence of previously generated tokens <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{&lt;i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{&lt;i}</annotation></semantics></math>. The softmax operation ensures that the output is a valid probability distribution over the vocabulary at time step <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(t_{i})=\text{softmax}(\mathcal{M}(P,T,I,t_{&lt;i}))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(t_{i})=\text{softmax}(\mathcal{M}(P,T,I,t_{&lt;i}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We define certainty as the minimum probability among the tokens in a proposed answer, where each token is selected as the model’s most likely output (i.e., the maximum probability at each step). For example, if the model predicts the answer "204" with token probabilities of 0.99 for ’2’, 0.98 for ’0’, and 0.99 for ’4’, the certainty of this answer is taken as the minimum of these values: 0.98.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{min-max}}=\min\left(\max_{i=1,...,n}p(t_{i})\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>min-max</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{min-max}}=\min\left(\max_{i=1,...,n}p(t_{i})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">To determine a suitable stopping threshold, we conducted empirical analysis across multiple runs, sweeping certainty values between 0.90 and 0.99. We found that certainty values above 0.97 reliably correlate with correct predictions, and selected 0.97 as our operational threshold. We chose to avoid values under 0.90 as that may lead to hallucinations and incorrect predictions.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.4 </span>Probing Mechanism and Answer Monitoring</h3>

<div id="S3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To apply the certainty criterion in real time, we implement a probing mechanism. Every 1,000 tokens, the model’s current output is examined to see if a candidate answer has been produced. If so, its certainty is computed. If the certainty exceeds the threshold (0.97), the model halts reasoning. Otherwise, it continues until the next probe point or until the token budget is exhausted.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This probing mechanism enables dynamic reasoning and provides multiple opportunities for answer revision. Notably, most answer changes occur within the early stages of reasoning, when the model’s internal reasoning state is still developing. Beyond this point, answers tend to stabilize, and probing becomes a reliable indicator of solution quality.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In most experiments, the same LLM type is used for both generating reasoning steps and for probing outputs. However, we also explored a configuration that introduces a secondary distinct model dedicated solely to analyzing outputs and estimating certainty.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This secondary model can vary in size and design: smaller models offer faster inference and lower deployment costs, making them attractive for real-time applications or API-based systems with usage constraints.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">On the other hand, larger or fine-tuned models may yield more accurate certainty estimates, especially if optimized for confidence calibration or specific evaluation tasks.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Additionally, the probing model does not need to share the same architecture as the reasoning model, allowing flexibility in selecting tools best suited for analysis. This modular setup is particularly useful in API-based workflows, where the primary model’s outputs can be post-processed by lightweight, locally run models to reduce latency and cost.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.5 </span>Combining Budget Forcing and Early exiting</h3>

<div id="S3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The pseudocode outlines the complete CGR procedure with budget forcing. The model <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> generates reasoning tokens up to a maximum budget <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, unless it reaches a high-confidence answer earlier.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">If the model attempts to terminate prematurely by emitting the special "<span id="S3.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;\thinking&gt;</span>" token, it is only allowed to stop if the current output passes a certainty threshold <math id="S3.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>. Otherwise, the stop attempt is overridden by inserting a "<span id="S3.SS5.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">\nWait</span>" token, forcing the model to continue reasoning.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In addition, the algorithm periodically probes the output every <math id="S3.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> tokens to check whether the current answer meets the confidence requirement. If so, the process halts early.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This approach dynamically balances compute efficiency and answer quality by allowing early exits for high-certainty answers while encouraging further reasoning when uncertainty remains.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg3" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 3</span> </span> Certainty-Guided Reasoning with Budget Forcing</figcaption>
<div id="alg3.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg3.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            Question <math id="alg3.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, Model <math id="alg3.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, Budget <math id="alg3.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, Certainty threshold <math id="alg3.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, Probe interval function <math id="alg3.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            Initialize output <math id="alg3.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
            Initialize token count <math id="alg3.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg3.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> <math id="alg3.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&lt;B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&lt;B</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
              Generate next token <math id="alg3.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\leftarrow\mathcal{M}(q,o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\leftarrow\mathcal{M}(q,o)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg3.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg3.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\texttt{&lt;/think&gt;}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">&lt;/think&gt;</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\texttt{&lt;/think&gt;}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>
<span id="alg3.l6.5" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg3.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Model tries to stop reasoning
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
               Compute certainty <math id="alg3.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\leftarrow\textsc{CertaintyProbe}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">CertaintyProbe</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\leftarrow\textsc{CertaintyProbe}(o)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
               <span id="alg3.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg3.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\geq\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\geq\theta</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
                 <span id="alg3.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">break</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
               <span id="alg3.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
              
                 <math id="alg3.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> “<span id="alg3.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">\nWait</span>” <span id="alg3.l11.4" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg3.l11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Force continue reasoning
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
              
              
               <span id="alg3.l12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg3.l12.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg3.l13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg3.l13.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
              
              
              Append token: <math id="alg3.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\leftarrow o\mathbin{\|}x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\leftarrow o\mathbin{\|}x</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="alg3.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leftarrow t+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leftarrow t+1</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">16:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg3.l16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg3.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(t)=True" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(t)=True</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l16.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17:</span></span>
              
              
               Compute certainty <math id="alg3.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\leftarrow\textsc{CertaintyProbe}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">CertaintyProbe</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\leftarrow\textsc{CertaintyProbe}(o)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l18.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">18:</span></span>
              
              
               <span id="alg3.l18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg3.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\geq\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\geq\theta</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l18.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l19.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">19:</span></span>
              
              
                 <span id="alg3.l19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">break</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l20.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">20:</span></span>
              
              
               <span id="alg3.l20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg3.l20.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l21.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">21:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg3.l21.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg3.l21.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l22.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">22:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg3.l22.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg3.l22.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l23" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l23.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">23:</span></span>
              
              
            Append <span id="alg3.l23.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">‘‘Final Answer: \boxed{’’</span> to <math id="alg3.l23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l24" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l24.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">24:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg3.l24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l24.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ExtractAnswer</span>(<math id="alg3.l24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math>)

</div>
<div id="alg3.l25" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l25.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">25:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg3.l25.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg3.l25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Results</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate our approach using the AIME2024 and AIME2025 datasets, comparing performance across three models: <span id="S4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-14B</span>, <span id="S4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Phi-4-reasoning-plus</span>, and <span id="S4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Qwen3-14B</span> (referred to as Deepseek, Qwen, and Phi4). We then shift our focus to the DeepSeek’s model, since its training cutoff date is estimated to be July 2024, with its release date in December 2024. This implies that there is no contamination with the AIME2025 dataset. To ensure reproducibility, all models were run at temperature 0 and seed 42.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Baseline Performance</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first analyzed the baseline performance of these models to see how they compare against each other.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 1</span>: </span><span id="S4.T1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Baseline performance on AIME2024.</span></figcaption>
<table id="S4.T1.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S4.T1.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
